### ❌ Fitting wheel — closed, won't build

**Labels:** `wontfix` `design`

Explored across five iterations: inline card overlay, enlarged variant,
wheel-first page rework, socket rails per group, single band.

Geometry was solved — chord clearance verified to 8 sockets, rack collisions
audited, `.ident` overlap and cover mask accounted for. The visual was not the
problem.

**Closed because** spatial arrangement is information a killboard reader
doesn't need. In-game the wheel exists because you interact with slots; nobody
clicks a socket on a kill page. The reference is a control surface, a kill page
is a record.

Also investigated and rejected: per-hull overlay maps stamped on the render
(hardpoint *positions* live only in the client's graphics resource files — not
in the SDE or ESI, no published dataset, ~500 hulls to hand-author);
class-level SVG schematics (discards the ship render); shape-morphing
silhouette (makes a false claim about the hull on every kill).

**Survives:** dropped/destroyed split rendered as an arc rather than a bar.
